module epics.`autonomous-nodes-and-mobile`

epic AutonomousNodesAndMobile {
  title "Autonomous nodes, seat keys and the phone: the swarm keeps working with the laptop closed"
  intent "Turn the single-Mac cockpit into autonomous nodes on a QUIC mesh over the user's tailnet, with our own seat key infrastructure and a phone that answers questions, in the phase order below, each phase landed and verified before the next."
  body """
    # Autonomous nodes, seat keys and the phone

    This is the entry point for the implementing worker. Read these first, in order:
    1. [[d1794292861627527-remote-nodes-round-2]], then [[d1794292861627529-remote-nodes-round-3]]. They supersede [[d1794292861627523-remote-nodes-round-1]].
    2. [[specs/nodes]]: the node, the mesh, the KB storage seam, Linux.
    3. [[specs/seat-keys]]: root, grants, `verify`, enrollment.
    4. [[specs/mobile]]: the phone as an addition to the desktop cockpit.

    The stand applies throughout ([[philosophy]]): subtract before you add, and each phase's report names what it removed.

    ## Outcome

    - The laptop closes, and seats on the other nodes keep working, messaging each other and writing the KB.
    - The phone answers their questions.
    - The laptop opens, and the desktop shows the current state with nothing restarted.
    - A Linux machine runs as a node and runs the UI.

    ## Phases, in landing order

    Each phase is one task, created when it starts.

    | # | Phase | Spec | Verification |
    |---|---|---|---|
    | 1 | Headless node on macOS and Linux; `make build-node`, `make test-linux` (dory, 2 CPUs, 4 GB) | nodes §1, §6, §10.1 | `make test-linux`; the node runs seats, harness, MCP and ctl with no window |
    | 2 | `bboxy450-seat-keys`: `Grant`, `Revoke`, `Rotate`, `verify`; the SeatKeyChain model | seat-keys §1–3, §8 | `cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-seat-keys && make test-formal` |
    | 3 | `bboxy450-mesh`: quinn, `peers.toml` (addresses only), root-pinned handshake, `bboxy/enroll/1`, `bboxy/gui/3` | nodes §2, seat-keys §5 | Two nodes (Mac and a dory container) list each other's seats; an unenrolled peer is refused |
    | 4 | `bboxy/pane/1` and `bboxy/blob/1`: remote panes render and steer | nodes §2, §5 | A pane on the other node steers mid-turn and resumes after a drop with no lost or doubled event |
    | 5 | `bboxy/msg/1`: `delivery.rs` and RemoteDelivery move into the mesh as MeshMsg; forwarded seat tools | nodes §3 | `make test-formal` (MeshMsg and its broken control); a cross-node message is delivered exactly once |
    | 6 | `KbStore` and the git replica over `bboxy/kb/1`; conflict records; the KbReplica model | nodes §4 | Two nodes edit one record offline and converge, with one conflict record |
    | 7 | Desktop inbox: `Questions`, `Answer` and the events; the first-answer rule; the QuestionAnswer model | mobile §3, §4, §7 | Desktop and phone fixture race on one item: one is `applied`, the other `already_answered` |
    | 8 | Retire `bboxy450-term-remote`, the `remote` profile, `remote_agent`, the ssh harness path, and the RemoteResume and RemoteRouting models; replace OpenPGP leaf certificates and `local-dev` with seat-keys | nodes §7, seat-keys §7 | The report counts the lines removed; `sh scripts/local-first.sh` holds |
    | 9 | Extract `bboxy450-client` from `live.rs`; the UI on Linux | mobile §6, nodes §6 | The Linux UI renders a Mac node's seats |
    | 10 | iOS shell (Inbox, QR enrollment), `apps/ios/`, `make ios-build`; Apple setup per mobile §6a | mobile §6, §6a | A device build answers a question on a node |
    | 11 | Push from nodes: `bboxy450-push` and APNs | mobile §5 | Laptop closed: push, answer, seat continues |
    | 12 | Overview and Glance; the `nodes-100-idle` gate | mobile §1, nodes §5 | `nodes-100-idle` holds |

    ## Superseded open tasks

    These open tasks came from the old ACP-over-ssh link. They are closed or re-scoped when phase 8 lands:
    - `tasks/2026-11-13-remote-session-migration` (historical, not in this KB): becomes stop, carry the log, then spawn with resume on another node.
    - `tasks/2026-11-13-acp-steering-parity` (historical, not in this KB): the code landed in harness `1436a01`; node seats steer natively.
    - `tasks/2026-11-13-remote-failure-classification` (historical, not in this KB), `tasks/2026-11-13-remote-artifact-pull` (historical, not in this KB) and `tasks/2026-11-13-remote-offload-icd-update` (historical, not in this KB): they become blob fetch and the node's own refusals.

    ## Rules for the worker

    - Every phase works in its own worktree and lands through `make land` with signed commits. Changed stateful contracts carry their model and a broken control (`make test-formal`).
    - Run one build or test at a time. Linux runs in one small dory container. Check `df -h` before any cold build.
    - Ask only for what is physical: the Apple steps in mobile §6a.
    """

